1
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:09,833
Dear May Deer,

2
00:00:09,833 --> 00:00:11,667
With a lovely family,

3
00:00:11,667 --> 00:00:15,250
Dreaming of growing up each day.

4
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:17,167
Shy Chuan-Chuan Pangolin,

5
00:00:17,167 --> 00:00:18,667
Quiet, with not a word to say,

6
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:19,667
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

7
00:00:19,833 --> 00:00:20,083
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

8
00:00:20,583 --> 00:00:21,667
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

9
00:00:21,833 --> 00:00:22,333
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

10
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:22,917
Don’t be shy!

11
00:00:23,083 --> 00:00:23,917
Don’t be shy!

12
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:24,500
Sing out loud!

13
00:00:24,667 --> 00:00:25,833
Sing out loud!

14
00:00:25,833 --> 00:00:27,417
Let your imagination shine!

15
00:00:30,583 --> 00:00:31,167
Good friends in the forest,

16
00:00:31,167 --> 00:00:33,083
Growing and playing together,

17
00:00:33,083 --> 00:00:34,000
Happy May Deer and Chuan-Chuan!

18
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,500
ODEER MAYO / Happy May Deer and Chuan-Chuan

19
00:00:37,676 --> 00:00:40,082
Off on a Camping Trip!

20
00:00:40,333 --> 00:00:42,583
It’s a beautiful, sunny day.

21
00:00:42,583 --> 00:00:44,667
The whole family is getting ready for their first camping trip.

22
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,750
Yay! We’re finally going camping! I’ve waited so long!

23
00:00:48,750 --> 00:00:51,833
Camping hat, camping bag,

24
00:00:51,833 --> 00:00:52,917
and camping magnifying glass!

25
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:55,750
Dad, are we there yet?

26
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:57,583
Haha! Almost there!

27
00:00:58,417 --> 00:01:01,833
We’re going camping somewhere really cool!

28
00:01:01,833 --> 00:01:04,333
Where are we going?

29
00:01:09,750 --> 00:01:10,000
Grandpa!

30
00:01:10,250 --> 00:01:11,250
Grandpa!

31
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:15,750
Hi, Grandpa!

32
00:01:15,750 --> 00:01:17,917
Ha! May, why the long face?

33
00:01:17,917 --> 00:01:19,583
So you’re camping at Grandpa’s house.

34
00:01:19,583 --> 00:01:21,500
What’s fun about that?

35
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:23,167
May!

36
00:01:23,167 --> 00:01:25,833
Silly girl! This is the ultimate camping spot.

37
00:01:25,833 --> 00:01:27,417
There are lots of treasures here!

38
00:01:27,417 --> 00:01:30,917
Treasures? Really?

39
00:01:31,333 --> 00:01:33,500
Grandpa, where’s the campsite?

40
00:01:33,667 --> 00:01:35,917
I’m ready to show what I can do!

41
00:01:39,750 --> 00:01:40,167
Hehe, we’re here!

42
00:01:40,333 --> 00:01:41,333
Hehe, we’re here!

43
00:01:43,333 --> 00:01:44,917
All right, make way!

44
00:01:44,917 --> 00:01:47,583
The first challenge of camping is setting up the tent.

45
00:01:57,083 --> 00:01:59,750
Oh, honestly. He’s still so stubborn.

46
00:02:00,583 --> 00:02:03,000
I’ll help you put up the tent.

47
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,083
All right.

48
00:02:04,083 --> 00:02:06,583
The great tent-building battle begins!

49
00:02:12,833 --> 00:02:15,083
Why does this look a little strange?

50
00:02:15,083 --> 00:02:15,583
Oh, dear!

51
00:02:16,333 --> 00:02:17,583
That’s strange.

52
00:02:17,833 --> 00:02:19,833
Dad, did we pull the tent fabric up too high?

53
00:02:20,391 --> 00:02:22,371
Okay, let's try again.

54
00:02:32,167 --> 00:02:33,833
Dad, is it too tight again?

55
00:02:34,417 --> 00:02:36,750
Is it? Let’s try again.

56
00:02:44,917 --> 00:02:47,333
All right! This time it’ll definitely work!

57
00:02:51,083 --> 00:02:53,500
Argh! Why can’t I get this tent up right?

58
00:02:54,250 --> 00:02:57,083
I think you’d better just read the instructions.

59
00:02:57,083 --> 00:02:58,667
Mm-hmm.

60
00:02:59,667 --> 00:03:00,000
Ooh! Ooh!

61
00:03:00,833 --> 00:03:02,667
I’m the Camping Fairy!

62
00:03:02,667 --> 00:03:04,833
Haha! Look, I’m a caterpillar!

63
00:03:05,167 --> 00:03:06,917
Now I’m a chubby fairy!

64
00:03:07,250 --> 00:03:10,167
Little Deer, look! I found a magic wand!

65
00:03:10,167 --> 00:03:11,833
Let’s put up our own tent!

66
00:03:11,833 --> 00:03:15,750
Abracadabra! Tent, stand up!

67
00:03:28,667 --> 00:03:30,167
That’s easy for me!

68
00:03:30,417 --> 00:03:33,250
Dad, you’re taking too long! Hurry up and light the fire!

69
00:03:34,583 --> 00:03:36,250
Oh, and one more thing…

70
00:03:36,250 --> 00:03:39,083
May, while we wait, let’s go treasure hunting with Grandpa.

71
00:03:45,750 --> 00:03:49,333
Grandpa, this is just a vegetable garden. What’s so special about it?

72
00:03:49,333 --> 00:03:52,000
Silly child. Come treasure hunting with me.

73
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,917
We have cucumbers here,

74
00:03:53,917 --> 00:03:58,333
rapeseed greens, spinach, beans, and tomatoes.

75
00:03:58,333 --> 00:04:00,250
Pick some yourself!

76
00:04:00,417 --> 00:04:03,333
All right, Little Deer! We’ve arrived at Vegetable Treasure Mountain!

77
00:04:06,417 --> 00:04:08,833
Haha! It’s Mr. Cucumber!

78
00:04:13,917 --> 00:04:15,667
It’s Lord Pea!

79
00:04:17,750 --> 00:04:19,750
Ha! This is King Pumpkin!

80
00:04:21,667 --> 00:04:23,333
Pepper! Pepper!

81
00:04:23,333 --> 00:04:25,417
It’s Princess Sweet Pepper!

82
00:04:27,750 --> 00:04:30,833
Success! We found a whole pile of treasure!

83
00:04:32,917 --> 00:04:35,917
Mom, we had a huge harvest! We found lots of treasure!

84
00:04:37,250 --> 00:04:40,583
Great! But Dad still hasn’t gotten the fire going.

85
00:04:43,667 --> 00:04:46,417
That’s strange. Why won’t this fire light?

86
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:53,917
Dad, are you sure you’re okay?

87
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:55,750
While we’re waiting,

88
00:04:55,750 --> 00:04:57,917
May, here’s your final mission.

89
00:04:57,917 --> 00:04:59,583
Assemble the chair!

90
00:04:59,833 --> 00:05:02,083
No problem! Leave it to me!

91
00:05:02,333 --> 00:05:04,583
Hmm. Something seems off.

92
00:05:08,833 --> 00:05:10,667
Ha! This should do it!

93
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:13,833
This is Dad’s throne!

94
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,667
The fire! The fire is lit!

95
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,250
That was easy!

96
00:05:19,917 --> 00:05:22,250
Honey, you finally did it!

97
00:05:24,083 --> 00:05:26,000
Vegetable Adventure Soup!

98
00:05:27,917 --> 00:05:31,083
It’s made with all the vegetables you picked yourselves.

99
00:05:31,417 --> 00:05:33,250
May, slow down.

100
00:05:33,250 --> 00:05:34,833
Don’t choke.

101
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:39,250
This is delicious! Why does it taste even better than at home?

102
00:05:39,250 --> 00:05:40,250
Yummy!

103
00:05:40,250 --> 00:05:41,583
Camping really isn’t easy,

104
00:05:41,583 --> 00:05:44,583
but it’s so much fun when everyone works together.

105
00:05:44,583 --> 00:05:47,667
That’s right. That’s the fun of camping!

106
00:05:47,667 --> 00:05:51,083
Exactly! Any time spent together as a family is a happy time.

107
00:05:51,083 --> 00:05:53,667
Camping is easy-peasy for me, too!

108
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:01,000
Dad, it’s because you’re too fat!

109
00:06:01,667 --> 00:06:02,000
Hahaha!

110
00:06:02,833 --> 00:06:06,000
So camping at Grandpa’s house can be lots of fun after all!

111
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,833
Hahaha!
